From 449cc196e8a96c45d287a90c63ea42f1d3ababa4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Van Tran <trantoanvan@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:03:16 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(inbox): Telegram push with decision buttons; Needs you /
 For your info tabs

- feat(telegram): inbox notifications in the member's DM; decision buttons

  A member who bound a Telegram bot gets every new inbox item in that bot's
  DM, like the WeCom smart bot's inbox push: what they mute in Multica's
  notification settings never becomes an item, so it is not sent either. The
  bot of the agent behind the item is preferred
  (FindChannelBindingForMemberOnAgentInstallation), else the member's newest
  binding. A mention carries its comment text.

  A new decision (patch 0008) now raises an inbox item "decision_requested"
  (action required) for the issue's member subscribers, else the workspace's
  owners and admins. In Telegram it carries one button per option; a press by
  the bound member answers the decision and posts the answer as their comment,
  exactly as the web panel does, so the issue's agent wakes. The polling loop
  now also takes callback_query updates.

- feat(inbox): "Needs you" and "For your info" tabs

  The active inbox shows one of two tabs. A row (an issue's notifications,
  grouped) is in "Needs you" when any of its unarchived notifications is
  marked above info by the server (action_required: assigned to you, a
  decision to answer, a run that failed; attention: an autopilot problem)
  and its issue is not done or closed; the rest is "For your info". The
  grouped row shows only the newest notification, often a comment, so the
  split reads every unarchived notification, not the row. It opens on
  "Needs you" while that holds anything; that count is red. Each "Needs you"
  row starts with a chip naming the notification that asks. Archive stays
  "Done"; filters apply inside the tab. Web only. Reference: OpenMausBot's
  Needs you / For your info / Done.

Patch-Id: inbox
